  ask:["Onset to peak (seconds: dissection, PE, pneumothorax; minutes: ACS), character, radiation, exertional relationship, sweating, vomiting, syncope.","Pleuritic, positional, reproducible by palpation (each argues against ACS).","Risk: age, smoking, diabetes, hypertension, lipids, family history, cocaine, prior CAD.","PE risk: immobility, surgery, cancer, oestrogen, leg symptoms, previous VTE.","Tearing pain to the back, Marfan, known aneurysm, hypertension (dissection)."],
