 land:[["Lateral epicondyle","Prominent lateral bony point","Common extensor origin; tender just distal in tennis elbow."],["Medial epicondyle","Prominent medial point","Common flexor origin; the ulnar nerve runs in the groove behind it."],["Olecranon","Point of the elbow","With the epicondyles forms an isosceles triangle at 90° (Hueter's triangle; a straight line in extension): distorted in dislocation, preserved in supracondylar fracture."],["Radial head","Rotates under the thumb 2 cm distal to the lateral epicondyle during pronation–supination","Tender after a fall on the outstretched hand: radial head fracture (look for the fat pad sign on X-ray)."]],
 rom:[["Flexion","140–150°"],["Extension","0° (up to 10° hyperextension)"],["Pronation","80°"],["Supination","80°"]],
 look:"Carrying angle, swelling (olecranon bursitis is localised; effusion fills the lateral para-olecranon hollow (between radial head, lateral epicondyle and olecranon)), deformity.",
